    {
      "id": "secure-coding-practices",
      "title": "Secure Coding Practices for Web Applications",
      "slug": "secure-coding-practices",
      "date": "2023-05-30",
      "year": "2023",
      "description": "Essential security practices for web developers.",
      "content": "Secure coding is the foundation of application security. This guide covers essential practices for building secure web applications from the ground up.\n\n## Input Validation\n\nAlways validate and sanitize user input:\n\n\`\`\`javascript\n// Validate email format\nfunction isValidEmail(email) {\n  const emailRegex = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/;\n  return emailRegex.test(email);\n}\n\n// Sanitize HTML input\nfunction sanitizeHTML(input) {\n  return input.replace(/[<>\"'&]/g, function(match) {\n    return {\n      '<': '&lt;',\n      '>': '&gt;',\n      '\"': '&quot;',\n      \"'\": '&#x27;',\n      '&': '&amp;'\n    }[match];\n  });\n}\n\`\`\`\n\n## Authentication and Authorization\n\n- Use strong password policies\n- Implement multi-factor authentication\n- Use secure session management\n- Apply principle of least privilege\n\n## Data Protection\n\n- Encrypt sensitive data at rest and in transit\n- Use HTTPS everywhere\n- Implement proper key management\n- Regular security updates\n\nSecure coding is an ongoing practice that requires constant learning and vigilance."
    },
    {
      "id": "incident-response-playbook",
      "title": "Building an Incident Response Playbook",
      "slug": "incident-response-playbook",
      "date": "2022-12-08",
      "year": "2022",
      "description": "Creating effective incident response procedures.",
      "content": "A well-defined incident response playbook is crucial for minimizing the impact of security breaches and ensuring quick recovery.\n\n## Incident Response Phases\n\n### 1. Preparation\n- Establish incident response team\n- Create communication plans\n- Set up monitoring and detection tools\n- Regular training and drills\n\n### 2. Detection and Analysis\n- Monitor for security events\n- Analyze and classify incidents\n- Document findings\n- Determine scope and impact\n\n### 3. Containment\n- Isolate affected systems\n- Prevent further damage\n- Preserve evidence\n- Implement temporary fixes\n\n### 4. Recovery\n- Remove threats\n- Restore systems\n- Monitor for recurring issues\n- Return to normal operations\n\n### 5. Lessons Learned\n- Document the incident\n- Analyze response effectiveness\n- Update procedures\n- Share knowledge with team\n\n## Key Tools\n\n\`\`\`bash\n# Log analysis\ngrep \"error\" /var/log/syslog\n\n# Network monitoring\nnetstat -an | grep LISTEN\n\n# Process monitoring\nps aux | grep suspicious_process\n\`\`\`\n\nHaving a solid incident response plan can mean the difference between a minor security event and a major breach."
    },
